From: Georg Seema <georgseema@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: default to the NSS 256 MiB profile on Cudy P5

The P5 has two NSS-offloaded radios and 256 MiB of RAM. Keep the extra
NSS allocation reductions enabled on both P5 layouts even when they
share the ath11k module with other IPQ50xx boards.

Check the board once during profile selection. Keep the existing
build option for other boards and the runtime checks for radio type,
the 256M profile and active NSS.

Signed-off-by: Georg Seema <georgseema@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -166,6 +166,8 @@
 	}
 
 	ab->mem_profile = &ath11k_mem_profile_params[profile];
+	ab->nss_256m = IS_ENABLED(CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MEM_PROFILE_256M) ||
+		       of_machine_is_compatible("cudy,p5");
 	ab->compact_rx_desc = ab->mem_profile->compact_rx_desc &&
 			      ab->hw_params.hw_ops->rx_desc_get_offset;
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
@@ -1128,6 +1128,7 @@
 
 	struct ath11k_hw_params hw_params;
 	const struct ath11k_mem_profile_params *mem_profile;
+	bool nss_256m;
 	/* the rx descriptor is used without its rx header TLV */
 	bool compact_rx_desc;
 
@@ -1467,7 +1468,7 @@
 /* Keep untested hardware and the host data path on their normal sizes. */
 static inline bool ath11k_nss_256m_enabled(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
-	return IS_ENABLED(CPTCFG_ATH11K_NSS_MEM_PROFILE_256M) &&
+	return ab->nss_256m &&
 	       ab->mem_profile->id == ATH11K_MEM_PROFILE_256M &&
 	       ab->nss.enabled &&
 	       (ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10 ||
